"A globe does not have this problem. A globe is a small model of the Earth with the same round shape, so the shapes of the lands, their sizes, the distances between places, and the directions from one place to another can all be right at the same time. But a globe is hard to carry, hard to print in a book, and it never shows you the whole world at once. So people flatten the globe. A map projection is a set of rules for moving every point on the round Earth to a point on a flat sheet.": "977281d49ae4",
