"Here is the trouble: something has to stretch. In the 1820s the mathematician Carl Friedrich Gauss proved a theorem which shows that the surface of a ball cannot be flattened without changing some of its distances. Mapmakers call this stretching distortion. A flat map can keep shapes right, or keep areas right, or keep some distances or directions right, but it can never keep all of them right everywhere.": "b1dee2c38aee",
